<p>A French soldier was killed and six others were injured in a drone attack on a base near Erbil in Iraq’s Kurdistan region, French officials said. French military statements cited in coverage said the site is used for counter-terrorism training with Iraqi counterparts. President Emmanuel Macron called the strike “unacceptable”. Reuters said Iranian drones carried out the attack, while other reports did not specify where the drones came from.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/tJGwi6hVf9mzxPk8lcLPZsvIAqJ8nvE2mnryIZXXiYVafyAIEMJij6apG6rwF_8oDatsqY-pQDcMFitI0iBRngRNdRmItuK5azrdcJ8ImgAzKFjrev2FnEIkyd23hLu9mV6QbbqE7G2HDnje2T8KHv-xdVV336v1z5wPnOKoGRiYXEJHEWiFRaWTAVL16_CGA17V35vlV-l5gHAz3ceDEhaLLQSf2bCNR3wXPhSIif13OiNMbeKs5RRQ-cQXQ29bXTTCaw' alt='Smoke rises from the site of a drone crash on the outskirts of Erbil, Iraq, March 12, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Named fatality: Macron identified the soldier killed as Chief Warrant Officer Arnaud Frion of the 7th Chasseurs Alpins Battalion in Varces.</li><li>Threat claim: A pro-Iranian armed group, Ashab Al-Kahf, said it would target “all French interests in Iraq and the region,” according to reports cited by Politico.</li></ul><blockquote>The war in Iran cannot justify such attacks. - Emmanuel Macron</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Emmanuel Macron (France): He called the strike “unacceptable,” said France’s deployment operates within a “strict framework” focused on counterterrorism and the fight against the Islamic State group, and said the war with Iran does not justify attacks on French forces in Iraq. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/french-soldier-killed-several-wounded-iraq-attack-emmanuel-macron-confirms/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>French military command: It said drones hit the base during a counter-terrorism training mission with Iraqi counterparts, and that the wounded were taken for medical treatment, without saying where the drones came from. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.